WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:17.122
Dr. Dolittle called a meeting with all the stowaways.

2
00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:21.625
"I am very disappointed in you, Jip," he scolded.

3
00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:25.908
"And you, too, Gub-Gub!"

4
00:00:25.928 --> 00:00:29.851
"We only wanted to go with you, Dr.

5
00:00:29.891 --> 00:00:31.732
Dolittle," the pig cried.

6
00:00:33.084 --> 00:00:36.947
"And I wanted to be part of your adventures," interrupted Matthew.

7
00:00:39.429 --> 00:00:41.110
Dr. Dolittle shook his head.

8
00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:45.773
"I'm afraid this trip is not an adventure, but a rescue mission."

9
00:00:45.793 --> 00:00:47.714
"To rescue whom?"

10
00:00:48.094 --> 00:00:48.795
asked Matthew.

11
00:00:49.555 --> 00:00:51.457
But the doctor did not explain.

12
00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:58.001
"Tommy," he said instead, "bring me the map."

13
00:00:58.021 --> 00:00:59.622
Tommy returned with the map.

14
00:01:00.863 --> 00:01:06.997
"Aha," said the doctor after a while, "Capa Blanca Islands."

15
00:01:08.178 --> 00:01:11.359
Everyone waited quietly for the doctor to continue.

16
00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:16.560
"We can stop there and drop off the stowaways," he said.

17
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.401
Dr. Dolittle turned the boat toward the north.

18
00:01:20.421 --> 00:01:22.882
"Is it very far from here?"

19
00:01:23.302 --> 00:01:24.042
Tommy asked.

20
00:01:24.062 --> 00:01:27.583
"Not too far," the doctor replied.

21
00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:32.621
"Polynesia!" he called, "how is the water temperature?"

22
00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.502
Polynesia pulled up her tail.

23
00:01:36.522 --> 00:01:39.604
At the end of her tail was a long piece of string.

24
00:01:40.824 --> 00:01:43.786
And tied to the end of the string was a thermometer.

25
00:01:43.806 --> 00:01:46.807
"Brrr!" she shivered.

26
00:01:46.827 --> 00:01:49.728
"The water feels cold."

27
00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:53.790
Polynesia held the thermometer close to her face.

28
00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.472
"I must be getting old," she sighed.

29
00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:01.377
"I can't see what it says."

30
00:02:02.798 --> 00:02:04.740
Tommy helped her read the thermometer.

31
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.362
"It looks okay," said Tommy.

32
00:02:08.382 --> 00:02:10.624
"Good," said Dr.

33
00:02:10.664 --> 00:02:16.448
Dolittle. "If the water temperature is very cold, there might be icebergs nearby."

34
00:02:18.089 --> 00:02:22.552
At that moment, there was a loud thump followed by a cracking noise.

35
00:02:22.573 --> 00:02:25.415
"The thermometer must be broken!"

36
00:02:26.075 --> 00:02:27.156
cried Polynesia.

37
00:02:27.808 --> 00:02:28.628
"Dr. Dolittle!

38
00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.649
Be careful!"

39
00:02:30.029 --> 00:02:30.849
shouted Tommy.

40
00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:32.489
But it was too late.

41
00:02:32.509 --> 00:02:35.970
Dr. Dolittle lost control of the wheel and fell.

42
00:02:36.931 --> 00:02:38.571
Tommy ran over to Dr.

43
00:02:38.611 --> 00:02:39.992
Dolittle to help him up.

44
00:02:40.012 --> 00:02:42.712
"Grab the wheel, Tommy!"

45
00:02:43.112 --> 00:02:44.153
the doctor shouted.

46
00:02:44.933 --> 00:02:47.354
Tommy tried but it was too heavy.

47
00:02:47.374 --> 00:02:50.074
"I can't see the iceberg, Doctor!"

48
00:02:50.455 --> 00:02:51.035
he gasped.

49
00:02:51.815 --> 00:02:53.996
"It must be underwater," Dr.

50
00:02:54.036 --> 00:02:54.996
Dolittle replied.

51
00:02:55.884 --> 00:03:00.845
There was another cracking sound and Tommy saw water leaking into the boat.

52
00:03:03.746 --> 00:03:05.887
Meanwhile, there was trouble in the kitchen.

53
00:03:05.907 --> 00:03:07.067
"Hurry, Chip!"

54
00:03:07.447 --> 00:03:08.228
yelled Charles.

55
00:03:08.248 --> 00:03:09.948
"My name is Jip!

56
00:03:10.308 --> 00:03:11.189
Not Chip!"

57
00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:12.409
barked the dog.

58
00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:16.530
But of course Charles could not understand animal language.

59
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.171
"Cover the holes with the potato sacks!"

60
00:03:19.571 --> 00:03:20.091
he cried.

61
00:03:20.931 --> 00:03:22.792
They blocked the water with the sacks.

62
00:03:24.932 --> 00:03:27.334
Soon the water seeped through the potatoes.

63
00:03:28.395 --> 00:03:29.776
"What should we do?"

64
00:03:30.117 --> 00:03:30.857
cried Charles.

65
00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.639
"I have an idea!"

66
00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:33.820
oinked Gub-Gub.

67
00:03:34.441 --> 00:03:37.843
But of course the humans only heard snorting sounds.

68
00:03:38.524 --> 00:03:39.405
"Use the flour!

69
00:03:39.745 --> 00:03:40.826
Like making bread!"

70
00:03:41.306 --> 00:03:42.187
the pig cried.

71
00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.691
"What are you talking about?"

72
00:03:47.152 --> 00:03:47.812
barked Jip.

73
00:03:48.973 --> 00:03:51.976
"I saw Dab-Dab do it," the pig explained.

74
00:03:52.712 --> 00:03:55.033
Gub-Gub opened the lid of one barrel.

75
00:03:55.053 --> 00:03:57.494
"What on earth is that pig doing?"

76
00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:58.775
shouted Matthew.

77
00:03:59.355 --> 00:04:02.156
He did not have fond memories of flour barrels.

78
00:04:04.437 --> 00:04:06.137
Gub-Gub pushed the barrel over.

79
00:04:06.998 --> 00:04:08.478
Flour came spilling out.

80
00:04:09.039 --> 00:04:12.220
Then, using a broom, he pushed it toward the holes.

81
00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.642
As the flour absorbed the water, it became sticky and thick.

82
00:04:17.302 --> 00:04:18.402
It turned into dough.

83
00:04:18.943 --> 00:04:20.363
The dough plugged the holes.

84
00:04:20.983 --> 00:04:22.204
"What a clever pig!"

85
00:04:22.632 --> 00:04:23.293
said Charles.

86
00:04:23.973 --> 00:04:26.835
Together they began emptying all the flour barrels.

87
00:04:29.056 --> 00:04:32.218
Soon the kitchen looked like a giant oven filled with dough.

88
00:04:32.899 --> 00:04:35.040
The water stopped leaking into the boat.

89
00:04:36.081 --> 00:04:39.383
"That should hold us till we get to land," said Matthew.

90
00:04:39.403 --> 00:04:45.286
"I'm quite impressed," Charles said as he handed Gub-Gub another biscuit.

91
00:04:45.987 --> 00:04:47.488
Gub-Gub snorted loudly.

92
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.441
After a while the boat was under control again.

93
00:04:52.461 --> 00:04:53.982
"What happened?"

94
00:04:54.322 --> 00:04:54.942
asked Tommy.

95
00:04:54.962 --> 00:04:58.784
"I think it must have been a rock," replied the doctor.

96
00:04:58.804 --> 00:05:03.946
"The boat's been damaged, especially in the kitchen," said Charles.

97
00:05:03.966 --> 00:05:10.009
"And we have no more flour," added Matthew, "and the potatoes are spoiled."

98
00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:12.490
Everyone's heart felt heavy.

99
00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.711
But soon their spirits lifted.

100
00:05:19.212 --> 00:05:19.552
"Land ho!"

101
00:05:19.572 --> 00:05:21.114
Polynesia called from the mast.

102
00:05:22.034 --> 00:05:23.376
They all stood up to look.

103
00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:26.378
Indeed, land was within sight.

104
00:05:26.398 --> 00:05:32.584
"We'll get our boat fixed," said the doctor happily, "and get some more food.

105
00:05:33.024 --> 00:05:36.567
Then we'll be on our way to Spider Monkey Island."
